    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The anatomical contour of the Distal Lateral Fibula plate is designed to support the surface of the lateral malleolus",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "7 hole distal cluster accepts 2.7mm variable angle locking screws to reduce the overall profile of the construct, reduce the potential for irritation, and allow for capture of articular fragments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomical plate contour may reduce the potential for malrotation by allowing center placement of the distal screw cluster over the lateral malleolus with shaft placement on the lateral face of the shaft",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Placement and screw trajectories are designed to allow for capture of distal and anterior fragments that avulse with the anterior syndesmotic ligaments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Variable angle ability of the screws so that surgeons can choose a trajectory for syndesmosis capture based on the fracture, their experience, preference and patient anatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed with the use of SOMA: Stryker Orthopedics Modeling and Analytics. 1",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The SOMA bone database contains a collection of 5570 and growing clinical CT scans and contains over 34,600 3D bone models.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The low profile 2.0mm distal end and 2.6mm shaft are designed to reduce the potential for soft tissue irritation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
